# Before you can verify credentials 

GOV.UK Wallet will allow trusted parties to verify and use credentials and attributes in person and online. There are systems in place to identify and authorise consumers of credentials. These will make sure personal data is only accessible to verified departments and organisations and not malicious apps or services.

To verify credentials from GOV.UK Wallet, you will need to:

* [get certified and registered](#get-certified-and-registered-as-a-dvs) as a Digital Verification Service (DVS)
* [onboard your service](#onboard-your-service-with-govuk-wallet) with GOV.UK Wallet
* [request an intermediate sub-CA certificate](#request-an-intermediate-sub-ca-certificate) to issue end-entity verifier certificates
* [use the sandbox](#verify-test-credentials) to verify test credentials
* [integrate with production](#verify-real-credentials) to verify real credentials

## Get certified and registered as a DVS

You will need to [join the register of digital identity and attributes services](https://www.gov.uk/guidance/join-the-register-of-digital-identity-and-attribute-services) by certifying against the [UK digital identity and attributes trust framework](https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/uk-digital-verification-services-trust-framework). This will demonstrate your organisation meets government standards as a safe, secure and reliable provider of digital verification services.

## Onboard your service with GOV.UK Wallet

Your DVS lead will need to [contact GOV.UK Wallet]() to onboard. An engagement manager will guide them through the process to integrate with the sandbox and production environments.

## Request an intermediate sub-CA certificate

You'll need to create and [send a certificate signing request (CSR)]() to your engagement manager. You'll need a separate CSR for each environment. GOV.UK Wallet certificate authority (CA) will check your CSR and issue you an intermediate sub-CA certificate. You can use your sub-CA to issue the [end-entity verifier certificate]() you need to present when consuming and verifying credential data. 

## Verify test credentials 

You can create and verify test credentials in the [sandbox environment](). To authenticate all the requests you make, you'll need to use the sub-CA issued for the sandbox environment.

## Verify real credentials

Once you have tested verifying credentials in the sandbox, you need to speak to your engagement manager about getting access to the production environment. You will need to use your intermediate certificate issued for production to validate requests for personal data from users.
